: "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19102, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01W8BbARuuXRsUnbYdgFkyDY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19102, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017wuC3bj1P9bDDy2FH6eCoD", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19402, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017wuC3bj1P9bDDy2FH6eCoD", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19402, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017wuC3bj1P9bDDy2FH6eCoD", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 23996, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01FD7iVLKDJYbgTpiFHR7zRb", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. Release history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc as unhealthy. The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0. The SRE agent started a rollback to v2.3.0. The first attempt partially failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving the service on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished in all regions. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54596, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FD7iVLKDJYbgTpiFHR7zRb", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54596, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FD7iVLKDJYbgTpiFHR7zRb", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 56256, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01A5iQhnZdYtbPiM64TF5oXK", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56556, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01A5iQhnZdYtbPiM64TF5oXK", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56556, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01A5iQhnZdYtbPiM64TF5oXK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 61783, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n1. **Choosing the version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. The two releases after it, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, are both unhealthy. Because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before, it didn't need change-manager approval.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error. Only us-east switched to v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. Repeating a rollback to the same version is safe, so I ran it once more and it finished in all regions.\n3. **Check:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. Health checks are passing, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to about 0.2%.\n4. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so there's only one incident and one page went out. INC-0001 is open and covers what happened and the rollback, including the partial failure and retry.\n\nTwo things in the incident still need looking into: why v2.3.1 failed, and what caused the orchestrator error during the first rollback attempt.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01N7QZe5SwjosrcpyWFmz9yk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0183E1QC9gvJGpgF2RkE8Ewg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1). Later releases v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both unhealthy. Rolling back now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NvcfK7EYyJEvBbCKGs93mq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VPDfFJchh7ANNTpKGzmoDL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback only finished in us-east. A rollback to the same version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry it once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013m8E7g2YaCEqh5U23kXcnk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01W8BbARuuXRsUnbYdgFkyDY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017wuC3bj1P9bDDy2FH6eCoD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FD7iVLKDJYbgTpiFHR7zRb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. Release history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc as unhealthy. The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0. The SRE agent started a rollback to v2.3.0. The first attempt partially failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving the service on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished in all regions. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01A5iQhnZdYtbPiM64TF5oXK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n1. **Choosing the version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. The two releases after it, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, are both unhealthy. Because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before, it didn't need change-manager approval.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error. Only us-east switched to v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. Repeating a rollback to the same version is safe, so I ran it once more and it finished in all regions.\n3. **Check:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. Health checks are passing, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to about 0.2%.\n4. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so there's only one incident and one page went out. INC-0001 is open and covers what happened and the rollback, including the partial failure and retry.\n\nTwo things in the incident still need looking into: why v2.3.1 failed, and what caused the orchestrator error during the first rollback attempt.", "type": "text"}]}]}